&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;SENIOR MATERIALS ENGINEER (METAL 3D PRINTING)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;Freeform builds AI-native manufacturing systems that unify software, hardware, and physics to produce industrial-scale parts at the speed of human ideation. By treating manufacturing as a single integrated system, we unlock a new era of innovation where complex hardware is designed, built, and scaled without limits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Materials Engineer at Freeform, you will have the unique opportunity to establish the company’s M&amp;amp;P infrastructure, strategy, and best practices for our advanced metal 3D printing technology. We are looking for someone with solid fundamentals in materials engineering, an understanding of metals, and a keen interest in working on the cutting edge of additive manufacturing development. In this role, you will own materials engineering efforts from cradle to grave, including hands-on sample testing, analysis of findings, and strategic process improvements. If you want to make an impact at a rapidly growing company that’s revolutionizing metal additive manufacturing, we’d love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success here doesn&#39;t hinge on 3D printing experience. Instead, we seek intelligent, motivated, and collaborative engineers who thrive on solving challenging problems and creating groundbreaking technology!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;iframe src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/sXfG6ssZ190?feature=shared&quot; width=&quot;560&quot; height=&quot;315&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish Freeform’s M&amp;amp;P best practices, and materials testing infrastructure and strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate equipment to measure material properties such as tensile strength, surface roughness, and microstructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate and track quality metrics of printed customer parts such as dimensional accuracy, defect distribution, and surface roughness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organize, analyze and interpret data and present key findings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with process development team to tie key materials findings into improvement of upstream printing processes, including training our advanced machine learning models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and optimize processes and procedures for measuring and quantifying material quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create automation for M&amp;amp;P procedures to take human out of the loop&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategize continuous improvement plans to enhance system performance, reliability, and scalability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in material science, materials engineering, metallurgy, or mechanical engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of professional materials engineering experience (with at least three years in metals)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and optimizing metallurgical sample preparation techniques such as cutting, grinding, polishing, acid etching, and optical microscopy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s or PhD in in material science, materials engineering, metallurgy, or mechanical engineering highly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of materials engineering experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with metal additive manufacturing highly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with laser powder bed fusion (LPBF) processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in process development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating complex materials equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with processing large datasets and statistical data analysis software such as R, JMP, or Minitab&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for improving the state of metal 3D printing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based in Hawthorne, our vertically integrated facility brings technology development, R&amp;amp;D, and production together under one roof. We operate at the center of LA’s deep tech ecosystem, surrounded by some of the most ambitious hardware innovation happening anywhere in the country.&lt;/p&gt;
